.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-31-#   dispatch itself stays argv-driven (see each router).
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-32-#
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-33-# Schema (per route):
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-34-#   command:          string — the doctor command that owns the route
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-35-#   target:           string — positional name the user types
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-36-#   yaml:             string — YAML asset filename in assets/
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-37-#   setup_vars:       list   — variables the router resolves and passes to YAML
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:38:#   allowed_flags:    list   — per-target flag schema (target-first parsing)
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:39:#   mutating:         enum   — read-only | add-only | mutates
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-40-#   gate3_location:   string — concrete mutation target (or "n/a" for read-only)
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-41-#   mcp_tools:        list   — subset of router's frontmatter allowed-tools union
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-42-#   trigger_phrases:  list   — diagnostic routing phrases for this target, three or
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-43-#                              more words each; the bridge deriver copies them
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-44-#                              into the advisor (see "Consumed by" above)
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-45-#   default_target:   bool   — optional; true marks the read-only target a bare typed command
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-46-#                              should suggest (the router's no-token target, or its read-only
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-47-#                              entry point), so /doctor:ci alone also reaches this route's
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-48-#                              advisor bridge. At most one per command, only on a command with
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml:49:#                              several targets, and never on a mutating route.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-50-#   lead_phrases:     list   — optional subset of trigger_phrases that puts this bridge ahead of a passing skill when the prompt contains the phrase. Use it only where the doctor command must lead the skill.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-51-#
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-52-# Skill-advisor recommendation tools are registered through system-skill-advisor.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-53-# To add a new target:
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-54-#   1. Append the route here with its owning command and trigger_phrases of three or more words. Add lead_phrases only for a phrase where the doctor command must rank above a passing skill.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-55-#   2. List the target in that command's router and presentation, and add its row to the /doctor:setup target list in .skilled/commands/doctor/assets/doctor-setup-presentation.txt.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-56-#   3. To let the advisor suggest it, add its activation entry to both the "typescript" and "python" lists in .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/scoring-compatibility.json. A bridge without one stays inactive.
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-57-#   4. Rerun node .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/command-bridges/derive-command-bridges.cjs, then bash .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/route-validate.sh and node .skilled/commands/doctor/scripts/doctor-phrase-reach.cjs.
--
.skilled/commands/doctor/_routes.yaml-59-# To remove a target: delete the route AND its corresponding assets/doctor-<target>.yaml.
